  "name": "TeamRetro: Park tagged Help Scout conversations for your next retro",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "91438a67-2fc3-481c-9fb0-1d1deb60a7a4",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -240,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 720,
        "height": 784,
        "content": "## TeamRetro: Park tagged Help Scout conversations for your next retro\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow listens for Help Scout conversations and only continues when a designated retro-related tag is present. It retrieves the conversation, extracts ticket details, uses an OpenAI-powered chain to classify and summarize the customer message, then checks whether the item is actionable. Actionable items are compared against recent TeamRetro parked items to avoid duplicates before either creating a new parked item or noting that the conversation was already parked.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Connect and authorize the Help Scout trigger and Help Scout action nodes with access to the relevant mailbox and conversations.\n- Configure the Help Scout tag condition in \"If Retro Tag Exists\" so only conversations intended for retrospectives enter the workflow.\n- Add OpenAI credentials for the chat model used by \"Summarize & Classify Ticket\" and confirm the structured output schema matches the downstream fields.\n- Connect TeamRetro credentials, then replace `REPLACE_WITH_TEAM_ID` with your team ID in **both** TeamRetro nodes (\"Fetch Recent Parked Conversations\" and \"Add to TeamRetro Park\").\n- Review the Help Scout note actions so they write appropriate internal notes back to the original conversation.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the retro tag name, the AI classification prompt/schema, and the token-overlap dedupe threshold (`THRESHOLD = 0.6` in \"Remove Token Overlap Duplicates\" — raise toward 0.8 if distinct items get swallowed as duplicates, lower it if near-duplicates slip through) to match how your team defines actionable retrospective items and duplicates."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "55305e95-a098-46c3-aa73-eb90640440ec",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        560,
        128
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 864,
        "height": 304,
        "content": "## Capture tagged conversation\n\nStarts from Help Scout, checks for the retro tag, fetches the full conversation, and extracts the ticket fields needed for later AI processing."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "03bc6dfd-ef55-46de-8581-02f7537b648c",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1440,
        128
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 528,
        "content": "## Classify customer feedback\n\nUses an OpenAI chat model with structured output parsing to summarize and classify the conversation, then filters out items that are not actionable."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f4a5af88-517c-4072-ab92-26b46fca10dc",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2032,
        128
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 304,
        "content": "## Check existing parking lot\n\nRetrieves recent TeamRetro parked items and runs a token-overlap dedupe check, then branches based on whether a similar item already exists."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a066a132-8457-43cf-ae1a-7385a9591bc0",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2704,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 416,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Park new retro item\n\nCreates a new parked item in TeamRetro for non-duplicate feedback and adds a confirmation note back to the Help Scout conversation."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "4fd929e1-00e0-4158-bcbb-ffd121835df3",
      "name": "Sticky Note5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2704,
        352
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 256,
        "height": 400,
        "content": "## Note duplicate item\n\nHandles the duplicate branch by adding a Help Scout note indicating the feedback was already parked for the retro."
